# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 038
# Act: DEF+  (Alteration aimed at Figure)   Stance: Dissecting   Site: Lens
#
# DEF's pass for the "anomalous" kind. Turn-21's frame, as revised by
# turn-29, explicitly names magnitude-anomaly as a candidate second member
# of "signal, not noise" — candidate, not yet a claim. This turn makes
# that claim, within the same frame, on the two anchored anomalous
# entities (turn-36) independently:
#
#   @cc38c3ae... IS "signal (magnitude-anomaly), not noise"
#   @186c8ea0... IS "signal (magnitude-anomaly), not noise"
#
# Named distinctly from turn-22's "signal, not noise" (absence-recurrence)
# rather than reusing the identical value string — DEF's own discipline
# (EO Event Streaming §6) treats these as genuinely different claims about
# different mechanisms, and collapsing the wording would quietly imply one
# mechanism licenses the other, which gap-033 already refused.
#
# What earns this claim: both entities cleared turn-31/turn-32's
# mechanism (a ground built from the other 31 values, distance in
# aperture-widths) at 96.04 and 62.49 widths respectively — far beyond
# noise-control's own -0.10 — and turn-35 already traced this recurring
# consistently across two independent instances. Still a claim, not a
# discovery: an agent is named, and it stays revisable.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-37 (anchored entities to claim
# about) and turn-29 (a frame that names this candidate member). Refuted
# if either entity's widths did not in fact exceed the control's — checked
# at turn-32/turn-34, both far exceed it.

:turn-38  eot:opens        :turn-37 .
:turn-38  eot:act          eot:DEF+ .
:turn-38  eot:stance       "Dissecting" .
:turn-38  eot:site         "Lens" .
